  "summary": "Unpacks a Trush stream read through SP (bytes and 16-bit bit words interleaved) upwards from the block's base + $CE, then moves the output down to end at the block's destination end (LD SP,IX, LDDR) and returns with interrupts enabled. Relative jumps only: the same bytes in every block but the output length (LD BC at Done).",
